-- title:
--   Idelic first-inequality data for a prime-degree Galois extension
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M/L$ be an extension of number fields (in a common universe) which is Galois with $[M:L]=p$, and let $\mathfrak f_0$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_L$ that is admissible at $p$ for $M/L$ in the sense of `IsAdmissibleModulusAt`: $\mathfrak f_0\neq 0$, and for every finite prime $v$ of $L$ for which the selected prime `primeAbove L M v` of $M$ has nontrivial inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(M/L)$, the power $v^{2e_v+1}$ divides $\mathfrak f_0$, where $e_v$ is the ramification index at $v$ of the ideal generated by $p$. The conclusion is `IdeleFirstIneqDataAt L M 𝔣₀`: there is a group homomorphism $N$ from the idele units of $M$ to those of $L$ such that (1) whenever an idele $u$ of $M$ and $\alpha\in M^\times$ satisfy `IsAdjuster` at the extended modulus $\mathfrak f_0\mathcal O_M$ (at each finite prime dividing that modulus the component of $u\alpha^{-1}$ has valuation $1$ and is congruent to $1$ to the exact exponent occurring in the modulus, and `archSign` holds at each real embedding of $M$), then $N(u)$ and $\mathrm{N}_{M/L}(\alpha)$ satisfy `IsAdjuster` at $\mathfrak f_0$; (2) the fractional-ideal content of the finite part of $N(u)$ equals `fracRelNormUnit` applied to the content of the finite part of $u$; (3) if $\mathfrak f_0$ satisfies `IsAdmissibleModulus` for $M/L$ (nonzero, with $v^{\mathrm{admissibleExp}\,v}\mid\mathfrak f_0$ at every $v$ with nontrivial inertia), then the subgroup `unitIdeles L 𝔣₀` lies in the range of $N$; and (4) $[M:L]$ divides the index of the subgroup of the ideles of $L$ generated by the principal ideles together with the range of $N$.
--
--   This packages the input to the first inequality of global class field theory (Chevalley's idelic form) for a cyclic extension of prime degree: the relative idelic norm together with its compatibility with moduli and with ideal contents, its surjectivity onto unit ideles of an admissible level, and the divisibility of the norm-class index by the degree. It feeds the computation of the index of the norm subgroup in the idele class group in prime degree and, through it, the prime-power case of the bound on the norm class index.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_PrimeNormIndex_ideleFirstIneqDataAt_of_finrank_eq_prime.lean

